---
title: "Decentralized Arisan with Blockchain"
date: "2025-11-10"
tags: ["Blockchain", "Solidity", "Smart Contracts", "Web3"]
---

## Overview

Exploring how Solidity smart contracts can bring transparency and trust to traditional rotating savings circles (arisan).

## The Problem

Traditional arisan groups face several trust issues:
- **Transparency** — members can't verify who paid what
- **Centralized control** — the organizer has full power
- **Disputes** — no immutable record of transactions

## The Solution

A smart contract that handles all arisan logic autonomously:

```solidity
contract ArisanChain {
    struct Member {
        address payable wallet;
        bool hasPaid;
        bool hasReceived;
    }

    Member[] public members;
    uint public contributionAmount;
    uint public currentRound;
}
```

## Smart Contract Features

- **Automated collection** — members send ETH directly to the contract
- **Random selection** — verifiable random winner selection each round
- **Immutable records** — all transactions are on-chain
- **No middleman** — the contract is the trust layer

## Why Blockchain?

The goal wasn't just to build an app, but to demonstrate how blockchain removes the need for a trusted third party in social financial systems.

